# Vision Studio backend - release runtime input (reviewed by hand).
#
# This is the ONE list of what the frozen backend bundle ships. It is not
# installed directly: `node build-backend.cjs --lock` compiles it into the
# per-platform, hash-locked runtime-<platform>.txt files beside it, and the
# release build installs ONLY those, with `pip install --require-hashes`.
#
# torch / torchvision are NOT listed here. They come from the PyTorch CUDA
# index (Windows/Linux) or PyPI (macOS) through their own hash-locked
# torch-<platform>-<flavor>.txt files; build-backend.cjs pins them in
# TORCH_PIN / TORCHVISION_PIN, and the lock step feeds that pin in as a
# constraint so every package below resolves against the torch that ships.
#
# Floors are security floors, not compatibility guesses - each names the
# advisory it clears. Raise them; never lower them.

# --- HTTP server ------------------------------------------------------------
